course: dictionary
lesson: 15440
title: Steadied: keeping still and calm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Steadied is the past tense of steady, so it tells us something happened earlier. Steady means firm, calm, or not moving about. «She steadied herself on the rail.» Here steadied means she made herself stop wobbling so she would not fall.
explain: The same word can describe a thing, a feeling, or a number. «He steadied the ladder while I climbed.» He held it still so it would not wobble. «He steadied his nerves before the test.» Here steadied means he calmed down.
explain: Clues in the sentence help you choose the meaning. «Prices steadied after a week of big rises.» The rises stopped, and the prices stayed about the same. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Steadied is the past tense of steady, so it means made steady or became steady in the past.
fact: «Steadied» can mean made something stop shaking or wobbling, as in «steadied the ladder».
fact: «Steadied» can mean became calm again, as in «steadied her nerves».
fact: In science and data, «steadied» means a reading stopped changing much, as in «the temperature steadied».
fact: Check the clues around the word: a wobbling object, a calm feeling, or a number that stops changing each point to a different meaning.
exercise: «She steadied herself on the rail as the boat rocked.» What does steadied mean here? | Ran away from the boat | Shouted for help | Painted the rail | *Made herself stop wobbling
exercise: «After the scare, he steadied his nerves with a deep breath.» What does steadied mean? | Ran faster | Got more nervous | *Calmed down | Lost his hat
exercise: «The temperature steadied at twenty degrees.» What does steadied mean? | *Stopped changing much | Got smaller | Went up and down wildly | Turned into ice
test: «He steadied the ladder while I climbed.» What does steadied mean here? | Climbed it very fast | Hid it behind the shed | *Held it still so it would not wobble | Painted it red
test: Which word is the past tense of steady? | steadies | steadiest | *steadied | steadying
exam: «Her hands steadied as she threaded the needle.» What does steadied mean? | Turned bright blue | *Became still and firm | Became very loud | Dropped the needle
